{
  "dom_id": "step-q106212",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266874/assets/3cda1fd58a124726ae5d616287f4b1c86d818ea8b82fc93c03e2cfea7a1e7740.png)\n\nThe graph of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ (shown above) has discriminant $D.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $D<0$\n\nII. $D>0$\n\nIII. $a>0$",
  "worked_solution": "Given the graph of a quadratic function:\n\n- if the graph has $2$ roots, then $D>0,$\n\n- if the graph has $1$ root, then $D=0,$ and\n\n- if the graph has no roots, then $D<0.$\n\nFor the given graph of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c:$\n\n- Notice that $a$ is the leading coefficient. Since the parabola opens upward, we have that $a>0.$ Therefore, statement III is true.\n\n- Also, notice that the parabola intersects the $x$-axis twice, so it has $2$ roots. Therefore, we must have $D>0.$ Hence, statement I is false, while statement II is true.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements II and III are true.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
